    Process Identification: Using ps -p [PID] -f and top to inspect running processes, PIDs, and system usage.

    Background Tasks: Running commands in the background using & and viewing active session tasks with jobs.

    Process Termination: Stopping processes using kill [PID] (polite SIGTERM) versus kill -9 [PID] (forced SIGKILL)
    Service Management (systemctl)

    Status & Verification: Checking service state with systemctl status [service] and systemctl is-active [service].

    Live State Changes: Using start, stop, and restart to alter running services immediately without affecting system boot settings.

    Boot Configuration: Using enable to ensure services launch automatically when the machine powers on, and disable to turn auto-start off.
